[h1]Big Copilot: the business dashboard Big Ambitions never gave you[/h1]
Ten shops, two warehouses, a factory and forty employees. Which business is losing money? Which shelf runs empty tomorrow? Who is about to quit? The game knows, but the answers are spread over a hundred screens. [url=https://bigcopilot.com]Big Copilot[/url] puts them on one board.

[b]Free, runs in your browser, no account.[/b]

[h2]What the board shows you[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Today:[/b] only what needs you now. Stock about to run out, staff whose demands are not met, a shop turning customers away at its ceiling, a factory standing idle.
[*][b]Every business ranked by profit,[/b] with its own page: trends, costs, customers by hour and the crew.
[*][b]Supply orders:[/b] what each shop really uses, what to import each week, and a checklist of the orders to change in the game.
[*][b]Staffing:[/b] a week of hours for each shop, ready to copy into BizMan. Nobody over the 12-hour limit, every station covered, and how many people to hire.
[*][b]Where to grow next:[/b] demand for every business type in every neighbourhood, and a location finder that ranks every free building by demand and foot traffic, with its estimated rent.
[*][b]A city map and a wiki:[/b] your businesses on the map, the game's help pages, and a setup guide for every kind of shop.
[/list]

[h2]What this mod adds[/h2]
Without the mod, Big Copilot reads a save file you pick. With it, the board reads the game you are playing and keeps up as you play.

[list]
[*]While a city is loaded, the mod hands the running game to Big Copilot in your browser, on your own PC.
[*]It refreshes every game hour, after every game save, and when you click Update.
[*]You no longer pick a save folder or look for the newest Recover save.
[/list]

[h2]New in 0.2.0: make the changes from the board[/h2]
The board can now make three changes in your game for you:
[list]
[*][b]Uniforms:[/b] set the default uniform wherever a role has none.
[*][b]Imports:[/b] apply the amounts from Plan imports to your import contracts.
[*][b]Staffing:[/b] write a shop's staffing plan into the game, for one shop or a run of shops.
[/list]
Every change shows what the game will do before you apply it and can be undone once. If the game has changed since the board last read it, the change is refused and nothing is written. The first change from a browser asks for your approval in the game; after that the browser is remembered.

[h2]How to use it[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe, then enable [b]Big Copilot Link[/b] in the game's Mods menu.
[*]Load a save.
[*]Open [url=https://bigcopilot.com]bigcopilot.com[/url] and click [b]Link to the game[/b]. Chrome and Edge ask once whether the site may connect to devices on your local network. That device is the mod on your own PC, so allow it.
[/olist]

[h2]Your data stays on your PC[/h2]
[list]
[*]The mod listens on 127.0.0.1:8322 only. Nothing outside your PC can reach it.
[*]It answers bigcopilot.com and pages on your own PC. Other websites get nothing.
[*]The board reads your company in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.
[*]The mod writes no files. It changes your game only when you apply a change on the board and approve that browser in the game.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]A save made with any mod enabled is a modded save. If you load an unmodded save with the mod on, the game asks "Load with mods?" and writes a copy named "(Modded)", leaving your original save as it was. The game turns bug reporting off for modded saves. That is the game's rule for every mod.
[*]The mod does nothing while the board is closed. It only refreshes when Big Copilot has asked in the last two minutes.
[*]Options, under Big Copilot Link in the game's mod options: switch it off, change the port (8322 to 8325), refresh every game hour, refresh when a building loads, forget approved browsers.
[*]Made for game build 3682, on Windows and macOS.
[/list]

